11","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Skye Kakoschke-Moore","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10854","person_slug":"skye-kakoschke-moore","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions - Higher Education - Funding","noes":27,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2017-09-14.46.1) introduced by Senator [Pauline Hanson](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/queensland/pauline_hanson). ### Motion text > *That the Senate notes the recent PhD thesis by Dr Greg Pazmandy, from the University of Technology Sydney, who found that:* > *(a) there is no association between Australian University rankings and the levels of, and changes, to Vice-Chancellor compensation;* > *(b) there is no association between financial performance measures of Government Business Enterprises and the levels of, and changes to, CEO compensation, even after controlling for their community service obligations; and* > *(c) the only explanatory variable associated with compensation for Vice-Chancellors and Chief Executive Officers is the size of the organisation.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4925","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2017-09-14/4"}
